articles.content_en:
Article 1: Where any of the following circumstances exists, it shall be deemed as “fabricating facts to defame others” as provided in paragraph 1 of Article 246 of the Criminal Law:
(1) Fabricating facts that damage others’ reputation and disseminating them on information networks, or organizing or instructing others to disseminate them on information networks;
(2) Tampering with original information content on information networks that involves others into facts that damage others’ reputation, and disseminating them on information networks, or organizing or instructing others to disseminate them on information networks;
Knowingly disseminating fabricated facts that damage others’ reputation on information networks, where the circumstances are flagrant, shall be treated as “fabricating facts to defame others”.

Article 2: Where any of the following circumstances exists in defaming others through information networks, it shall be deemed as “serious circumstances” as provided in paragraph 1 of Article 246 of the Criminal Law:
(1) The same defamatory information has actually been clicked or viewed 5,000 times or more, or has been reposted 500 times or more;
(2) Causing serious consequences such as mental disorder, self-harm, suicide, etc. to the victim or their close relatives;
(3) Having previously received an administrative penalty for defamation within two years, and then defaming others again;
(4) Other circumstances that are serious in nature.

Article 3: Where any of the following circumstances exists in defaming others through information networks, it shall be deemed as “seriously endangering social order and national interests” as provided in paragraph 2 of Article 246 of the Criminal Law:
(1) Triggering mass incidents;
(2) Causing public order chaos;
(3) Triggering ethnic or religious conflicts;
(4) Defaming multiple persons, resulting in severe adverse social impact;
(5) Damaging the national image and seriously endangering national interests;
(6) Causing severe adverse international impact;
(7) Other circumstances that seriously endanger social order and national interests.
